{
  "caseId": "averitec-dev-0010",
  "atoms": [
    {
      "id": "atom-1",
      "text": "Donald Trump, when he thinks of climate change, he says hoax.",
      "sourceText": "Donald Trump, when he thinks of climate change, he says hoax. Well, guess what? Speaking of hoaxes, remember what he said about these increasing violent hurricanes and the frequency?",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 182
    },
    {
      "id": "atom-2",
      "text": "He actually said, maybe we should detonate a nuclear bomb over the Atlantic.",
      "sourceText": "Donald Trump, when he thinks of climate change, he says hoax. Well, guess what? Speaking of hoaxes, remember what he said about these increasing violent hurricanes and the frequency? He actually said, maybe we should detonate a nuclear bomb over the Atlantic. By the way, the same stable genius who said the biggest problem we had in the Revolutionary War is we didn’t have enough airports.",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 390
    },
    {
      "id": "atom-3",
      "text": "The same stable genius who said the biggest problem we had in the Revolutionary War is we didn’t have enough airports.",
      "sourceText": "the same stable genius who said the biggest problem we had in the Revolutionary War is we didn’t have enough airports.",
      "start": 272,
      "end": 390
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "atomId": "atom-1",
      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-a9e260356e8f::sentence-53",
          "documentId": "doc-a9e260356e8f",
          "text": "About 3 weeks after Trump's 2016 election, National Geographic published an article titled, \"Nuking Hurricanes: The Surprising History of a Really Bad Idea.\" ",
          "start": 5565,
          "end": 5723
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-a9e260356e8f::sentence-46",
          "documentId": "doc-a9e260356e8f",
          "text": "- Trump called this story \"ridiculous\" in a Monday tweet from the G7 summit. ",
          "start": 4535,
          "end": 4612
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-a9e260356e8f::sentence-40",
          "documentId": "doc-a9e260356e8f",
          "text": "- The sources said that Trump's \"bomb the hurricanes\" idea — which he floated early in the first year and a bit of his presidency before John Bolton took over as national security adviser — went nowhere and never entered a formal policy process.\n",
          "start": 3415,
          "end": 3661
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-1389236b080c::sentence-12",
          "documentId": "doc-1389236b080c",
          "text": "But Trump said he wasn't letting the rain dampen his spirits about the event.\n",
          "start": 1708,
          "end": 1786
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-1389236b080c::sentence-6",
          "documentId": "doc-1389236b080c",
          "text": "Trump, speaking to reporters on the White House lawn en route to his property in Bedminster, New Jersey, acknowledged Friday he had some technical problems because of the soggy conditions during his speech.\n",
          "start": 861,
          "end": 1068
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-1389236b080c::sentence-2",
          "documentId": "doc-1389236b080c",
          "text": "President Donald Trump — who used to mock predecessor Barack Obama for using the devices during speeches — said Friday that technical problems with the teleprompter during his \"Salute to America\" led to his head-scratching remarks about the Continental Army securing not-yet existent \"airports\" during the Revolutionary War.\n",
          "start": 34,
          "end": 359
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "atomId": "atom-2",
      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-a9e260356e8f::sentence-31",
          "documentId": "doc-a9e260356e8f",
          "text": "\"They start forming off the coast of Africa, as they're moving across the Atlantic, we drop a bomb inside the eye of the hurricane and it disrupts it. Why can't we do that?\" the source added, paraphrasing the president's remarks.\n",
          "start": 2060,
          "end": 2290
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-a9e260356e8f::sentence-49",
          "documentId": "doc-a9e260356e8f",
          "text": "The notion that detonating a nuclear bomb over the eye of a hurricane could be used to counteract convection currents dates to the Eisenhower era, when it was floated by a government scientist.\n",
          "start": 4712,
          "end": 4906
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-a9e260356e8f::sentence-55",
          "documentId": "doc-a9e260356e8f",
          "text": "- Dropping a nuclear bomb into a hurricane would be banned under the terms of the Peaceful Nuclear Explosions Treaty between the U.S. and the former Soviet Union. ",
          "start": 5761,
          "end": 5924
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-1389236b080c::sentence-9",
          "documentId": "doc-1389236b080c",
          "text": "One of those moments was in the passage about 1775, he said.\n",
          "start": 1276,
          "end": 1337
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-1389236b080c::sentence-2",
          "documentId": "doc-1389236b080c",
          "text": "President Donald Trump — who used to mock predecessor Barack Obama for using the devices during speeches — said Friday that technical problems with the teleprompter during his \"Salute to America\" led to his head-scratching remarks about the Continental Army securing not-yet existent \"airports\" during the Revolutionary War.\n",
          "start": 34,
          "end": 359
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-1389236b080c::sentence-7",
          "documentId": "doc-1389236b080c",
          "text": "\"We had a lot of rain. I stood in the rain. The teleprompter went out,\" he said in response to a question from NBC's Kelly O'Donnell. ",
          "start": 1068,
          "end": 1202
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "atomId": "atom-3",
      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-1389236b080c::sentence-2",
          "documentId": "doc-1389236b080c",
          "text": "President Donald Trump — who used to mock predecessor Barack Obama for using the devices during speeches — said Friday that technical problems with the teleprompter during his \"Salute to America\" led to his head-scratching remarks about the Continental Army securing not-yet existent \"airports\" during the Revolutionary War.\n",
          "start": 34,
          "end": 359
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-1389236b080c::sentence-3",
          "documentId": "doc-1389236b080c",
          "text": "\"In June of 1775, the Continental Congress created a unified Army out of the Revolutionary Forces encamped around Boston and New York, and named after the great George Washington, commander in chief,\" Trump said during his address Thursday — although the army was not named after Washington. ",
          "start": 359,
          "end": 651
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-a9e260356e8f::sentence-54",
          "documentId": "doc-a9e260356e8f",
          "text": "It found, among other problems, that:\n",
          "start": 5723,
          "end": 5761
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-1389236b080c::sentence-9",
          "documentId": "doc-1389236b080c",
          "text": "One of those moments was in the passage about 1775, he said.\n",
          "start": 1276,
          "end": 1337
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-a9e260356e8f::sentence-48",
          "documentId": "doc-a9e260356e8f",
          "text": "The big picture: Trump didn't invent this idea. ",
          "start": 4664,
          "end": 4712
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-a9e260356e8f::sentence-33",
          "documentId": "doc-a9e260356e8f",
          "text": "- Trump replied by asking incredulously how many hurricanes the U.S. could handle and reiterating his suggestion that the government intervene before they make landfall.\n",
          "start": 2408,
          "end": 2578
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
